rthwest with two termini (Seattle and Portland) west of Spokane\n- Paragraph 37: C&M Subdivision - railway line between Chicago and Milwaukee; carries \"Empire Builder\" and \"Hiawatha Service\"\n\nSo the connection is:\n- Empire Builder runs on C&M Subdivision (Paragraph 37)\n- Empire Builder runs between Chicago and Pacific Northwest (Paragraph 1)\n- Empire Builder has two termini: Seattle and Portland (east of Chicago, west of Spokane, after Split Rock/Menominee, St. Paul, Minneapolis/St. Paul, St. Cloud, Wayzata, Duluth, Staples, Wisconsin Dells, Wausau, Marshfield, La Crosse, Green Bay, Ashland, Stevens Point, Cherry Valley (Bayfield), Superior, Minnesota-Duluth, Wausau, Marshfield, La Crosse, Green Bay,两只终止点 Seattle and Portland\n\n所以答案是：\n- Empire Builder\n- 是的，它在芝加哥和太平洋西北部之间运行\n- 2个终点站（Seattle和Portland）\n</think>\n\nBased on the documents provided, I can trace the multi-hop connection:\n\n1. **Which train serves both routes?**\n   - From Paragraph 37: The **Empire Builder** runs on the C&M Subdivision\n   - From Paragraph 1: The **Empire Builder** runs between Chicago and the Pacific Northwest\n\n2. **Does it run between Chicago and the Pacific Northwest?**\n   - **Yes**, explicitly confirmed in Paragraph 1\n\n3. **How many termini does it serve?**\n   - From Paragraph 1: The Empire Builder serves **two termini** - **Seattle and Portland** (both west of Spokane on the Pacific Northwest route)\n\n**Answer Summary:**\n- **Train:** Empire Builder\n- **Route:** Chicago to Pacific Northwest ✓\n- **Termini count:** 2 (Seattle and Portland on the westbound segment, plus Milwaukee on the Chicago route)\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_21c1387a6ffegai5izO9BknIMT","model":{"modelID":"qwen35-9b","providerID":"local"},"truncated":false},"title":"Search documents for train on C&M subdivision","time":{"start":1777645418578,"end":1777645437071}}}}
